@startuml correction-dependency-contract
' Dependency contract for hierarchical correction: a one-directional, acyclic
' crate DAG. Solid = mandatory path-dependency; dashed = optional / feature-gated.
' duallity is drawn detached (muted) because libgrammstein does not depend on it.
' The note on libgrammstein names the two ways it feeds the language-model
' dimensions to lling-llang.
' Render: plantuml -tsvg docs/diagrams/correction-dependency-contract.puml
' Source of truth for Figure 7 in docs/integration/lling-llang/hierarchical-correction.md §7.
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam rectangle {
  FontColor white
  FontStyle bold
  BorderColor #263238
  roundCorner 12
}
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ArrowFontColor #37474F
title Dependency contract — one-directional & acyclic (dashed = optional / feature-gated)

rectangle "**libgrammstein**\nLM factory + HierarchicalCorrector\n+ LevenshteinCorrectionLayer" as gram #2E7D32
rectangle "**lling-llang**\nWFST host: Lattice, layers,\ncompose, viterbi / nbest" as llang #6A1B9A
rectangle "**liblevenshtein**\nLevenshtein Transducer\n+ Zompist phonetics" as lev #1565C0
rectangle "**libdictenstein**\nDictionary traits +\nPersistentVocabARTrie" as dict #37474F
rectangle "**duallity**\necosystem Levenshtein->WFST adapter\n(NOT a libgrammstein dependency)" as dual #90A4AE

gram --> lev : mandatory
gram --> dict : mandatory
gram ..> llang : opt · feature\nlling-llang-integration
llang ..> lev : opt (levenshtein)
llang ..> dict : opt (lattice)

dual .[#90A4AE,dashed].> lev : ecosystem
dual .[#90A4AE,dashed].> llang : ecosystem

note right of gram
  libgrammstein feeds lling-llang two ways:
  (a) implements lling-llang's LanguageModel trait
      (score_sequence / score_continuation) via
      GrammsteinLanguageModel → LanguageModelLayer
  (b) NgramWfstExport::to_ngram_transducer::<W>()
      produces an lling-llang NgramTransducer with
      backoff ε-arcs (for cascade composition)
end note

note bottom of llang
  lling-llang has **no** libgrammstein dependency.
  Modified Kneser-Ney lives in libgrammstein;
  lling-llang's asr/ngram.rs uses Katz backoff.
end note

legend right
  | Colour | Crate |
  |<#2E7D32> | libgrammstein |
  |<#6A1B9A> | lling-llang |
  |<#1565C0> | liblevenshtein |
  |<#37474F> | libdictenstein |
  |<#90A4AE> | duallity (ecosystem, not a dep) |
endlegend
@enduml
